            {
                "entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                "word": "Chinaman",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "21ac7b38-a77d-4455-98d2-26274253d288",
                        "entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Chinamen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                        "entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A Chinese person, or person of Chinese descent."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "offensive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8aa9fdab-1961-4f7c-a4e5-1f1288e00faf",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "A disorderly Chinaman is rare, and a lazy one does not exist. So long as a Chinaman has strength to use his hands he needs no support from anybody; white men often complain of want of work, but a Chinaman offers no such complaint; he always manages to find something to do.[…]Any white man can swear a Chinaman’s life away in the courts, but no Chinaman can testify against a white man."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4998416-6a7a-43c9-b6c2-745204112d36",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "Another favorite pastime of the Highbinder who is usually a loafer, is to levy blackmail on a wealthy Chinaman.[…]If it were not that the Chinamen kill only men of their own race and let alone all other men, the citizens of San Francisco would have sacked and burned Chinatown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f83c0123-9bbb-4136-8402-45e913bccfc3",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "On the flat behind the mill, dawn-rising Chinamen shogged with nimble bare feet under their yoke-linked watering-cans. These busy brethren, meeting sometimes on the same narrow track, would pause, ant-like, seemingly to dumbly regard one another and their burdens, then, still ant-like, pass silently to their work."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9e4ad37-62c6-40de-b0a5-f6ee5d8d0e96",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "\"It is my fly-trap!\" shrieked the Chinaman. \"And I am the god of destruction!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d343c4a2-864a-45e5-a84c-2789637300f8",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "The carts rattle by, swinging from side to side; two Chinamen lollop along under their wooden yokes with the straining vegetable baskets—their pigtails and blue blouses fly out in the wind."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e321613a-9742-4bad-8cac-b06023f6ac92",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "1941, George Ade, Stories of the Streets and of the Town: From the Chicago Record 1893 - 1900, reprinted as 2003, Stories of Chicago, page 163,\nIn Clark Street, where all the nations of the earth dwell together in harmony, one has but to go downstairs to find a Chinaman. And when found he is washing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92ccef7f-6d74-4949-8d93-16d34a6a8aa0",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "America it's them bad Russians.\nThem Russians them Russians and them Chinamen. And them Russians."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e399e9f9-95e5-45e0-b36a-34471b6e67e1",
                                "sense_id": "18aa1249-40e0-3aff-8779-45cef2d5b106",
                                "text": "Diner Employee: How long you been standing there, you freak?\nDiner Customer: What are you, a Chinaman?\nXavier (Vernon Chatman): I wish I knew myself.\nDiner Employee: We don't cotton to strange Chinamen with no sense of self who stand secretly by for indeterminate amounts of time. Gonna put you in a world of hurt."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e623516-04e3-311b-9894-1cac9a81a21e",
                        "entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sailing ship of the 18th and 19th centuries engaged in the Old China Trade"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6028847a-c640-3eac-bbda-9a3852ed1ccd",
                        "entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Addiction from a narcotic, especially heroin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "obsolete",
                            "offensive",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6055df92-47ed-49c9-8b89-d6118df7110b",
                                "sense_id": "6028847a-c640-3eac-bbda-9a3852ed1ccd",
                                "text": "Chinaman half in and half out of the door. Codeine and goof balls, and complete discouragement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1ad8fba4-0d5e-4c43-b91f-88e891ed08fc",
                        "source_entry_id": "e040bbf4-afa4-33e0-8f2e-8b3c9dae2d90",
                        "source_sense_description": "a man who is Chinese, a Chinese man",
                        "target_lang_word": "Chinois",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Chinois",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                        "entry_id": "ecdfca95-a1b7-3e04-be51-e8ddb15c923f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Habitant de la Chine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1c889977-40b3-45b1-b005-9e2c4a4fe545",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "Mais je ne sais en vérité où trouver des expressions pour rendre ma pensée, ou plutôt pour traduire celle qui se loge dans l’étrange cerveau des Chinois."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a99517d-97f2-4f37-8197-60f7bf20b96c",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "Les Chinois tiennent pourtant avec beaucoup de soin des états statistiques et des relevés de dénombremens ; mais il y a des classes nombreuses qui ne sont pas comprises dans les recensemens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b2180020-a12d-4d29-ad62-dad865b4af1c",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "Pour en revenir aux Chinois, j’affirme qu’ils ont une compréhension vive, une facilité d’assimilation étonnante. Je les ai vus à l’œuvre, et j’en parle par expérience."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eb85a5d-740b-40e3-91bc-2be2bdf7f2d9",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "C’est vers le milieu du XIᵉ siècle que parait avoir été établie la première exploitation de la houille dans les environs de Newcastle en Angleterre, du moins en ce qui concerne l’Europe, car, d’après les récits des missionnaires, les Chinois se seraient servis de ce combustible bien avant notre ère."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d4715a8e-9cd8-4568-88ca-cf0f0216ab7a",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "Le long des boutiques éclairées, des ombres se succédaient sans hâte. Il y avait des nègres, quelques Chinois, des blancs. Tous reluquaient les filles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c362069-b6d2-4af2-9f73-cc964cba6c9c",
                                                "sense_id": "ba5234d5-8011-3ff5-abe1-40011c36adab",
                                                "text": "Et ce petit univers grouille de cancans, d'intrigues, de projets, d'ambitions, qui dépassent rarement le cadre de la sous-préfecture. Vous croyez que la Chine existe, vous ? Comment peut-on être Chinois ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06cd6c71-2b05-3f5a-bced-48c970491f5d",
                                        "entry_id": "ecdfca95-a1b7-3e04-be51-e8ddb15c923f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Han, membre de l’ethnie majoritaire chinoise."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9788d59-ab70-3293-8b2a-55e3cf7d39d5",
                                        "entry_id": "ecdfca95-a1b7-3e04-be51-e8ddb15c923f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "parfois Asiatique."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
